  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance for Shelter and Non-food Items for Flood-Affected Populations in the Dosso Region, Doutchi Department.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project provides urgent humanitarian assistance to flood-affected populations in the Dosso region of Niger. In response to heavy rains and floods that displaced over a million people, the project focuses on distributing emergency shelter kits and essential non-food items to 2,200 households, benefiting approximately 15,400 individuals. The intervention targets the most vulnerable communities in the Department of Doutchi, addressing immediate shelter needs and improving hygiene conditions with the provision of jerrycans, soap and hygiene kits, including menstrual hygiene materials.</narrative>
  </description>
